      "writtenOn": "2024-07-24T20:53:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of encoding all image props at this level, it would nicer to piggy-back on existing image asset support:\n\n  - assume all referenced images are in `assets`\n  - expect just a `refId` at this level to point to an asset\n  - then I think you should be able to use `AnimationBuilder::ScopedAssetRef` and `AnimationBuilder::loadFootageAsset` to locate and parse the asset, similar to how it\u0027s done in FootageLayer.cpp",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 158,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 163,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "5f2c969825b8b0cd0e2395b6f1ea2daa49b0e27a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a2b9cfff_b1fd7b65",
        "filename": "modules/skottie/src/effects/SkSLEffect.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 168,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-24T20:53:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can lookup child effects by name using `SkRuntimeEffect::findChild`, it seems we should be able to do something similar to `buildUniformData`.\n\nJust need to store more info in `fChildren`: name, shader, optional type (would allow treating the layer content case in a similar manner) - then we should be able to write the equivalent `buildChildEffectData` that allocates a zero-initialized vector of `SkRuntimeEffect::ChildPtr`s (size given by `SkRuntimeEffect::children().size()`), iterates over `fChildren`, looks up child metadata and then stores the child shader at the right vector index.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 165,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 168,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "5f2c969825b8b0cd0e2395b6f1ea2daa49b0e27a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a7289842_c5c028bd",
        "filename": "modules/skottie/src/effects/SkSLEffect.cpp",
